{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Only by pride</b> — On account of the presumption by which a man presumes against his fellow, the presumptuous one produces strife and contention, meaning, presumption drags strife along." "<b>they take counsel together</b> — they counseled not to act presumptuously; with them is wisdom. And את is like עם."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {1 "The syntax of שיעצו שלא יעשו בזדון is compressed; read literally as 'they counseled not to act presumptuously.' The referent of the implied subject is ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:32.034270985Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}